From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000003 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guruswamy Basavaiah <guruswamy.basavaiah@broadcom.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kpatch: guard NULL section in is_dynamic_debug_symbol

is_dynamic_debug_symbol() dereferences sym->sec->name for every STT_OBJECT
symbol without checking sym->sec. An undefined/external STT_OBJECT symbol
(SHN_UNDEF) has sym->sec == NULL, so create-diff-object segfaults when
kpatch_correlate_symbols() -> is_special_static() -> is_dynamic_debug_symbol()
is called for such a symbol. This is reached on CONFIG_CFI_CLANG kernels once
the __cfi_/__pfx_ prefix handling lets correlation proceed (e.g. diffing
fs/proc/meminfo.o).

A symbol with no section is not a dynamic-debug descriptor (those live in the
__verbose/__dyndbg sections), so guard sym->sec and treat it as non-matching.

Signed-off-by: Guruswamy Basavaiah <guruswamy.basavaiah@broadcom.com>
---
--- a/kpatch-build/create-diff-object.c
+++ b/kpatch-build/create-diff-object.c
@@ -349,9 +349,11 @@
 {
 	if (sym->type == STT_OBJECT && !strncmp(sym->name, "__rap_hash", 10))
 		return false;
-	if (sym->type == STT_OBJECT && !strcmp(sym->sec->name, "__verbose"))
+	if (sym->type == STT_OBJECT && sym->sec &&
+	    !strcmp(sym->sec->name, "__verbose"))
 		return true;
-	if (sym->type == STT_OBJECT && !strcmp(sym->sec->name, "__dyndbg"))
+	if (sym->type == STT_OBJECT && sym->sec &&
+	    !strcmp(sym->sec->name, "__dyndbg"))
 		return true;
 	if (sym->type == STT_SECTION && !strcmp(sym->name, "__verbose"))
 		return true;
